1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:05,000
Every night, when you close your eyes, your brain begins a strange journey.

2
00:00:05,500 --> 00:00:10,000
For thousands of years, people believed that dreams were messages from another world.

3
00:00:10,500 --> 00:00:15,000
Scientists today have a different explanation.

4
00:00:15,500 --> 00:00:21,000
They think dreams help the brain sort through memories and emotions from the day.

5
00:00:21,500 --> 00:00:27,000
During deep sleep, your body rests, but your mind stays surprisingly busy.

6
00:00:27,500 --> 00:00:33,000
The images in dreams can be wild and illogical, yet they often feel completely real.

7
00:00:33,500 --> 00:00:39,000
Some researchers believe that dreaming is a form of overnight therapy.

8
00:00:39,500 --> 00:00:45,000
Difficult experiences are replayed in a calmer chemical environment.

9
00:00:45,500 --> 00:00:51,000
Little by little, the sharp edge of a painful memory begins to fade.

10
00:00:51,500 --> 00:00:56,500
So the next time you wake up from an unusual dream, do not worry.

11
00:00:57,000 --> 00:01:00,000
Your brain is simply doing its housekeeping.
